# Code owners: GitHub asks these accounts to review pull requests that touch the matching paths.
#
# Kept to one entry on purpose. The only account that both owns this repository and appears in its git history as a
# maintainer is the repository owner, so it owns everything. Other names in the history are not listed because
# their write access to this repository is not established, and GitHub ignores (and flags) owners without it.
# When the team adds people or moves the repo to an organisation, give the sensitive paths their own owners, e.g.
#   /.github/            @<org>/platform
#   /deploy/  /scripts/deploy/   @<org>/platform
#   /backend/utilities/auth*     @<org>/security
#
# Do not turn on "Require review from Code Owners" in branch protection while every author and reviewer posts
# through this same account: GitHub never lets a pull request's author satisfy that rule, so no PR could merge.

